        "question_title": "The line \\(\\vec r=(1,2,3)+\\lambda(2,-1,1)\\) intersects the plane \\(x+y+z=9\\) at \\(P\\). Find the distance from \\(A=(1,2,3)\\) to \\(P\\).",
        "question_instruction": "Choose one correct option.",
        "explanation": "A point on the line is \\((1+2\\lambda,2-\\lambda,3+\\lambda)\\). Applying the plane equation gives \\(6+2\\lambda=9\\), hence \\(\\lambda=\\frac{3}{2}\\). Therefore, \\(AP=|\\lambda|\\sqrt{2^2+(-1)^2+1^2}=\\frac{3\\sqrt{6}}{2}\\).",
